RF.put("questb:b15",{"8655":{"id":8655,"t":"Avenger's Greaves","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 9,950, 0.66 times as much.","obj":"Bring the Qiraji Bindings of Dominance, 2 Idols of the Sage, 5 Bronze Scarabs and 5 Clay Scarabs to Kandrostrasz in Ahn'Qiraj. This quest also requires Neutral faction with the Brood of Nozdormu.\nQiraji Bindings of Dominance Viscidus in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Princess Huhuran in Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n2 Idol of the Sage Vekniss Soldier 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Stinger 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Bronze Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Clay Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 0 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","desc":"Qiraji magic is strong and ancient. The most powerful qiraji wield items of such might, they'd give pause even to a dragon.\nBring me the qiraji bindings of dominance and other minor components and I'll create a set of powerful boots for you.\nYou will find them useful in the fight against the enemy.","rew":"You will receive:\nAvenger's Greaves\nExperience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"You've acquired the items I requested, ‹name›?","done":"You've done well, ‹name›. You've proven you're no ordinary mortal.\nI give you these with the confidence they'll aid you in crushing the vile qiraji.\nStart Kandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple End Kandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Alliance Class Paladin Type Raid Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8655\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 13,200 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Mortal Champions\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] Avenger's Greaves this quest\nBring the Qiraji Bindings of Dominance, 2 Idols of the Sage, 5 Bronze Scarabs and 5 Clay Scarabs to Kandrostrasz in Ahn'Qiraj.\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP","cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8495":{"id":8495,"t":"The Alliance Needs More Iron Bars!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 20 iron bars to Corporal Carnes at the airfield in Dun Morogh.\n20 Iron Bar","desc":"Back so soon? Stop making me re-evaluate my low opinion of you ‹class›, you're making me feel all gooey inside. So, as you can tell we still don't have enough iron bars for all of the weapons, armor, steam tanks and whatnot that need building for the bug hunt. Think you have it in you to bring back another stack of twenty iron bars in between all of those trips to Zul'Gurub, or wherever it is that you kids hang out these days?","rew":"You will receive:\n5 Alliance Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","back":"Back so soon? Stop making me re-evaluate my low opinion of you, ‹class›, you're making me feel all gooey inside. So, as you can tell we still don't have enough iron bars for all of the weapons, armor, steam tanks and whatnot that need building for the bug hunt. Think you have it in you to bring back another stack of twenty iron bars in between all of those trips to Zul'Gurub, or wherever it is that you kids hang out these days?","done":"Must be a cold day in the Burning Steppes. Look here, it's ‹name›, and she's brought me a gift. Twenty iron bars! Just what I always wanted.\nIn all seriousness though, thank you, ‹name›. You're a credit to yourself and the Alliance. Now get back out there and bring in more stuff for the war effort!","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":61.5,"y":31.6,"n":"Corporal Carnes","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"655":{"id":655,"t":"Hammerfall","lv":34,"min":29,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Tor'gan in Hammerfall.","desc":"It is still clear to me, like yesterday... So many years without hope, with wood and steel to bind me to this terrible place. Then finally, finally! There was the Warchief. Doomhammer in his midnight plate, his warhammer held high.\nIt was... too terrible... That the blow of a coward would strike down our greatest hero. From behind he charged on his horse, and then his lance ran him through... I fell to my knees. What hope was there? What hope is there...","rew":"Experience: 270\n+25 reputation with Orgrimmar","done":"Ah, Gor'mul you speak of. Yes, from what he says, it seems he has never recovered from the death of Doomhammer.\nGor'mul was a captive here when Thrall and Orgrim fought to free the camp, but as the earth shook and our brethren escaped, he was left behind. He wandered alone and lost for years without direction or hope, until we returned to establish ourselves here in Hammerfall.","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":72.6,"y":33.9,"n":"Gor'mul","s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":74.7,"y":36.3,"n":"Tor'gan","e":1}],"cats":["arathi-highlands"]},"1055":{"id":1055,"t":"Raene's Cleansing","lv":28,"min":18,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to Shael'dryn at the moonwell.","desc":"The rod, now complete, lies in your hands. Shael'dryn will want to hear of your success.","rew":"Experience: 230\n+25 reputation with Darnassus","done":"You've done it, ‹name›! Well done!","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":56.4,"y":49.2,"n":"Hidden Shrine","s":1},{"z":"Ashenvale","x":53.5,"y":46.2,"n":"Shael'dryn","e":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"5535":{"id":5535,"t":"Spiritual Unrest","lv":47,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Destroy 6 Highborne Apparitions and 6 Highborne Lichlings before returning to Loh'atu in Azshara.\nHighborne Apparition slain : 0/ 6\nHighborne Lichling slain : 0/ 6","desc":"Long ago, the Highborne were some of the most powerful students of the arcane the night elves ever produced. The corruption that comes along with such studies caused much harm to night elf society and greatly affected all of Azeroth... as I'm sure you well know.\nI promised the Sentinels that I would release the spirits from their mortal bonds as I find them. If you would do the same, then I am sure I can reward you some.\nThe spirits haunt the Shadowsong Shrine to the northeast of here.","rew":"Money: 50 0 gold, 50 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,200","back":"How goes your search for the Highborne spirits, ‹class›?\nMany events have caused all the races of Azeroth great suffering, but for some reason, these spirits seem to be a plague for all people. Perhaps it is there continued desire for any arcane magic--such desire is a harbinger of the Burning Legion, and we know what that can lead to.","done":"Well done, ‹class›. Thank you for your help. The spirits are at peace, and the threats that their desire for the arcane draw have been lessened.\nI am sure that both sides of the conflict that ravishes Azeroth will see you are above such things.","pins":[{"z":"Azshara","x":11.4,"y":78.2,"n":"Loh'atu","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["azshara"]},"8575":{"id":8575,"t":"Azuregos's Magical Ledger","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver Azuregos's Magical Ledger to Narain Soothfancy in Tanaris.\nMagical Ledger\nProvided: Magical Ledger","desc":"You cannot understand a single word on this ledger. You don't even know what language it is written in!","rew":"Experience: 6,600\n+10 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"Ooooh! Magical pulsing thingy! For me?","done":"<Narain eagerly examines the letter.>\nOutstanding, ‹race›! What is it? I can't read a lick of Draconic.","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":65.2,"y":18.6,"n":"Narain Soothfancy","e":1}],"cats":["azshara"]},"735":{"id":735,"t":"The Star, the Hand and the Heart","lv":44,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return the items on the Bonegrip's Note to Gerrig Bonegrip in Ironforge.\nStar of Xil'yeh Grel'borg the Miser\nHand of Dagun Dagun the Ravenous\nThe Legacy Heart Mogh the Undying\nProvided: Bonegrip's Note","desc":"Yagyin's Digest, eh? Are you starting a new chapter of us, somewhere? Never mind, it is not my place to ask.\nI will help you, for I have an extra copy. We must aid each other, yes? That is how we flourish.\nI require three items of power. Bring them to me and I will give you the digest.\nI will not speak their names. Ears may be on us. But here, I will write them down.","rew":"Experience: 5,600","back":"Do you have the relics for which I asked?","done":"You are resourceful, ‹class›. If it truly is your charge to begin a new chapter of our order, then I believe you will run it well.\nDun Morogh Alterac Mountains Dustwallow Marsh Stranglethorn Vale","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":59.2,"y":22,"n":"Gerrig Bonegrip","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["badlands"]},"4735":{"id":4735,"t":"Egg Collection","lv":60,"min":57,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 8 Collected Dragon Eggs and the Collectronic Module to Tinkee Steamboil at Flame Crest in the Burning Steppes.\n8 Collected Dragon Egg\nCollectronic Module\nProvided: Collectronic Module","desc":"‹name›, I'm finally ready for real samples of dragon eggs! Here, take this collectronic module. It's designed to extract a dragon egg and prepare it for transport. Go back to the Rookery and use the module to collect eggs.\nAnd don't forget to freeze them first, or they might hatch before you can collect them!\nWhen you have enough eggs, bring them to me!","rew":"Money: 2 70 2 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Steamwheedle Cartel","back":"Do you have the eggs, ‹name›? My patron heard you were collecting them for me, and is very eager to get his hands on them!","done":"Wow, you got them! The collectronic module worked! I'm a genius!\nThank you, ‹name›. My patron will be very pleased to get these eggs...","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":65.2,"y":24,"n":"Tinkee Steamboil","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blackrock-spire"]},"96655":{"id":96655,"t":"Camping 101 cooking","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Cook Torka in Razor Hill to learn to become a cook.\nLearn cooking from Cook Torka in Razor Hill","desc":"So you want to learn more about camping, huh? Good for you, ‹class›. The first step any adventurer needs to take is to become a cook and learn how to make a campfire.\nCooking's not just about making tasty foods. It's also the foundation for your camp.","back":"A good campfire is the foundation to any good camp.","done":"With this, you'll be able to set up a camp anywhere out in the wilderness. What you've learned is just the basics, so you won't be able to place too many furnishings around it.\nRaise your cooking skill and you might just be able to learn to make even bigger fires.\nYou can also learn the basics of furnishing your campsites from other tradeskill trainers if you're savvy in their skills.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":52,"y":47.4,"n":"Brakk","s":1},{"z":"Durotar","x":51.2,"y":42.4,"n":"Cook Torka","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"97935":{"id":97935,"t":"Camping 101 mining","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Brek Stonehoof in Thunder Bluff to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your mining skill to 20","desc":"Mining isn't the most glamorous, but it's good honest work and a fine profession for you to explore.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Lodestone for your camp. Build one of these and everyone who wants to swing a sword will be eager to gather round your fire and soak up the extra \"oomph\" it can provide to increase their combat prowess.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Lodestone. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.\nMulgore Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":46.2,"y":67.2,"n":"Kaga Wildhoof","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":34.6,"y":57.6,"n":"Brek Stonehoof","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94335":{"id":94335,"t":"Craftsmans writ green lens","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Green Lens\nGreen Lens","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Green Lens, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Green Lens Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94335","cats":["crafting"]},"94255":{"id":94255,"t":"Craftsmans writ spider silk slippers","min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet. Partly read from what players of our addon saw in game.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Spider Silk Slippers\nSpider Silk Slippers","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting 1 Spider Silk Slippers, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin Pouch\n+75 reputation with Azeroth Commerce Authority\n+75 reputation with Durotar Supply and Logistics","back":"Yo!","done":"Are these my new boots?\n<Kixxle looks very excited, but it fades immediately upon setting his eyes upon them.>\nAh. I thought I had cancelled the order for slippers once I realized how foolish it would be to trudge around a swamp with my toes hanging out. I ordered a new pair of proper boots too, but they still haven't arrived yet.\nOh well, pleasure doing business with you. I'll keep these for later!","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":50.1,"y":37.7,"n":"Kixxle","e":1}],"cats":["crafting"]},"7935":{"id":7935,"t":"10 Tickets - Last Month's Mutton","lv":60,"min":25,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Item #19182","rew":"You will receive:\nLast Month's Mutton","back":"Step right up, step right up! If you have tickets from the Darkmoon Faire you'd like redeemed, then just say so! You can redeem tickets in various denominations for wondrous and fantastic prizes. Don't be shy, give it a try!\nItem #19182 (10)","done":"Here you go, here you go! A prize fit for a king! Congratulations to you, my friend!\nIf you have more tickets you'd like to turn in, then please let me know! For as long as the Darkmoon Faire is here, I'll redeem your tickets.\nMulgore Elwynn Forest","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":38.2,"y":44.7,"n":"Gelvas Grimegate","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":41.5,"y":68.9,"n":"Gelvas Grimegate","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkmoon-faire"]},"98895":{"id":98895,"t":"Darkspear islands clash","lv":39,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring 3 Darkspear Islands Marks of Honor to an Alliance Brigadier General outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Darkspear Islands Mark of Honor","desc":"The battle against the Darkspear Raiders is heating up. Without urgent aid, the Darkspear Islands will be lost to us.\nIt is your duty as a proud member of the Alliance to ensure this does not happen. Bring me proof of your contributions on the front lines and you will be revered as a hero of the Alliance!","rew":"Money: 45 0 gold, 45 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,500\n+150 reputation with Theramore Expeditionary Force\nAlterac Mountains Arathi Highlands Ashenvale Stormwind City Ironforge Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":39.4,"y":82.2,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":45.6,"y":45.8,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Ashenvale","x":61.8,"y":83.8,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":79.4,"y":18,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Ironforge","x":69.8,"y":90,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":58,"y":34.4,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkspear-islands"]},"1375":{"id":1375,"t":"Khan Shaka","lv":37,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Maintain your reputation with the Magram, and bring the Head of Khan Shaka to Warug in the Magram Village in Desolace.\nKhan Shaka's Head Khan Shaka\nReach 3000 reputation with Magram Clan Centaur","desc":"You help the Magram, and I like you. Now, kill the Khan of the Gelkis! He is Khan Shaka, and I want his head! I want to stare at his head and laugh at him!","rew":"Experience: 2,850","back":"Do tasks for the Magram, and I will help you.","done":"Khan Shaka is dead! I will place his head on a pike, and keep it with me so Shaka can see the strength of the Magram!","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":75,"y":68.2,"n":"Warug","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"1455":{"id":1455,"t":"The Karnitol Shipwreck","lv":39,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to Kreldig Ungor in Desolace.","desc":"You take a few moments to figure out what pried the chest open, and you notice along the sides and top of the chest, long, deep scratches that reveal that something other than a man or giant took interest in it. The marks don't appear as if they were caused by dagger or sword.\nAfter going through the chest you find it to be completely empty.\nNot having another course of action, you close the chest and prepare to leave. Kreldig will be disappointed.","rew":"Experience: 1,500\n+50 reputation with Ironforge","done":"Welcome back to Nijel's Point, ‹name›. So, tell me what you found.\nWhat!? Nothing? An empty chest ain't gonna get us paid, I'm afraid.\nTell me more about these marks you saw... these slashes.","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":36.1,"y":30.5,"n":"Karnitol's Chest","s":1},{"z":"Desolace","x":66.2,"y":9.6,"n":"Kreldig Ungor","e":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"415":{"id":415,"t":"Rejold's New Brew","lv":10,"min":8,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Rejold Barleybrew.","desc":"Rejold Barleybrew at Brewnall Village has been asking for you.\nHe wants to talk to you about a new drink he's been brewing...said something about you helping him with it. You might want to head back to Brewnall Village and see what he has to say.\nThere could be some free booze in it for you...","rew":"You will receive:\nMug of Shimmer Stout\nExperience: 85\n+10 reputation with Ironforge\n+10 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","done":"‹name›! You know that Shimmerweed you brought me? Well I used it in a few recipes I've been working on, and one of them turned out great!\nHere, try it out and tell me what you think...","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":46,"y":51.7,"n":"Tharek Blackstone","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":30.2,"y":45.7,"n":"Rejold Barleybrew","e":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"815":{"id":815,"t":"Break a Few Eggs","lv":8,"min":6,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Taillasher Eggs to Cook Torka in Razor Hill.\n3 Taillasher Egg Taillasher Eggs","desc":"Bah! I almost forgot I need to get breakfast ready.\n‹name›, get yourself movin' and get me some taillasher eggs. I'll need at least three of them if I'm going to have enough for tomorrow's meal.\nThe Bloodtalon taillashers can be fierce, and protect their eggs to the death more often than not. They sometimes bury their eggs too deep in the earth to uncover safely, but if you head to the Echo Isles to the southeast of Sen'jin Village, you can usually find them all over those islands.","rew":"You will receive:\n5 Tough Hunk of Bread 5 Tough Jerky\nMoney: 2 25 0 gold, 2 silver, 25 copper Experience: 700\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Breakfast, lunch, dinner! Who cares which meal it is? It still has to be cooked by someone--namely me!","done":"You might be weak, but at least you're not clumsy, ‹name›.\nHere, take this and get outta my way. I've got cooking to do.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":51.1,"y":42.4,"n":"Cook Torka","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"175":{"id":175,"t":"Look To The Stars","lv":25,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Renamed from Look To The Stars.","obj":"Locate Mary and persuade her to give up a reflective surface for Viktori's project.","desc":"According to Cog's blueprint, what I need now is a way to reflect light. I remember a woman by the name of Mary who became well known around these parts for always carrying a looking glass. Perhaps you can track Mary down and see if she might lend us a reflective surface for this project? I believe she once resided in southern Duskwood. . .","rew":"Experience: 1,000","done":"Why yes, I used to own a looking glass.","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":79.8,"y":48,"n":"Viktori Prism'Antras","s":1},{"z":"Duskwood","x":82,"y":59.1,"n":"Blind Mary","e":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"95":{"id":95,"t":"Sven's Revenge","lv":25,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Go to Sven's Farm and find what was buried behind the old stump.","desc":"I used to work one of the farms to the southeast...until Dark Riders from Deadwind Pass descended upon my farm and slaughtered my family when I was away!\nWhen I returned I saw a shadowy figure skulking near my barn, burying something. He fled before I could catch him, and I couldn't linger for I was hot on the heels of the Dark Riders. So I never discovered what was hidden.\nIf you can find what that shadowy figure buried, I would be grateful. The hiding spot is behind the old stump near my barn.","rew":"Experience: 1,000\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","done":"A mound of dirt is here, hastily piled up as if someone had need of hiding something...without much time to do it.","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":7.8,"y":34.1,"n":"Sven Yorgen","s":1},{"z":"Duskwood","x":49.9,"y":77.7,"n":"Mound of loose dirt","e":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"1135":{"id":1135,"t":"Highperch Venom","lv":30,"min":25,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 Highperch Venom Sacs to Fiora Longears in Theramore.\n10 Highperch Venom Sac Highperch Patriarch 80 % , Highperch Consort 80 % , Highperch Wyvern 80 % , Heartrazor 80 %","desc":"As you may know, wyverns are often tamed by orcs for use as mounts. But what is less known is that the venom of a wyvern, in some circles, is more valuable than the beast itself. So if you're not afraid to do a little wyvern hunting, then... I have a job for you.\nThere is a place called Highperch in the land of a Thousand Needles, west of here. The Highperch wyverns have a potent venom. Potent, and valuable.","rew":"You will receive:\nWindborne Belt\nExperience: 3,650","back":"Did you find Highperch, ‹name›? Any luck with the wyverns there?","done":"Ah, most of these are nearly bursting with venom, ‹name›. Such are normally only gathered from young wyverns, or fertile females. It must have been quite a slaughter up there in Highperch!\nDustwallow Marsh Thousand Needles","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":66.5,"y":45.1,"n":"Fiora Longears","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"15":{"id":15,"t":"Investigate Echo Ridge","lv":3,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 10 Kobold Workers, then report back to Marshal McBride.\nKobold Worker slain : 0/ 10","desc":"‹name›, my scouts tell me that the kobold infestation is larger than we had thought. A group of kobold workers has camped near the Echo Ridge Mine to the north.\nGo to the mine and remove them. We know there are at least 10. Kill them, see if there are more, then report back to me.","rew":"Money: 40 0 gold, 0 silver, 40 copper Experience: 250\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Have you been to the mines? Are you ready to report?","done":"I don't like hearing of all these kobolds in our mine. No good can come of this. Here, take this as payment, and when you're ready, speak to me again. I would like you to go back to the mines one more time...","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":48.9,"y":41.6,"n":"Marshal McBride","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"91775":{"id":91775,"t":"Book return","lv":6,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Find 6 Lost Books and \"Fun with Elementals\" and return them to Marshal Dughan.\nPicture Book: Fun with Elementals\n6 Lost Book","desc":"While you're investigating the Fargodeep Mine, see if you can find any of Brother Paxton's books to return. In particular, Paxton is very concerned about a book titled, \"Fun with Elementals\". He thinks even a kobold could use it to summon an elemental servant. Be warned, the depths of the mine are fairly dangerous. You should bring friends.\nTake this book bag to protect the books when you find them!","rew":"You will receive:\nBook Bag\nMoney: 2 50 0 gold, 2 silver, 50 copper Experience: 675\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Have you found all the books yet?","done":"I applaud your diligence, Pawtrik. Brother Paxton sent a list of books, and you've found most of the missing ones. The rest must have been taken to the Jasperlode Mine.\nYou can keep that book bag!","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":42.2,"y":65.8,"n":"Marshal Dughan","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"98815":{"id":98815,"t":"Highland hides","lv":28,"min":24,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Return 4 Thicket Raptor Hides to James Halloran, the tanner, in Menethil Harbor.\n4 Thicket Raptor Hide","desc":"The Highlands are host to ruins of some sort, secrets now being explored by an expedition team. What I know is that they've got their own wildlife and beasts lurking in that mountain marshland. How about you take a foray in there with some well-equipped friends, and we work a trade?\nI don't care if they're hiding, I want their hides! Bring me the skins from four of the Thicket Raptors, I'll have a trade worked out for you to make it worth it.","rew":"Money: 12 0 gold, 12 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,150\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":8.6,"y":55.6,"n":"James Halloran","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["excavation-site-wetlands"]},"2975":{"id":2975,"t":"The Ogres of Feralas","lv":43,"min":38,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Rok Orhan in Camp Mojache wants you to kill 10 Gordunni Ogres, 10 Gordunni Ogre-Magi, and 5 Gordunni Brutes.\nGordunni Ogre slain : 0/ 10\nGordunni Ogre Mage slain : 0/ 10\nGordunni Brute slain : 0/ 5","desc":"The effects of the Gordunni Ogre tribe can hardly go unnoticed in this area. Look around, ‹name›; their very presence scars this land. We must push them back before they expand even further into Feralas.\nFollow the river north, and you will find their outpost. Decrease their numbers, ‹name›. We must show them that their kind is not wanted here.","rew":"Money: 45 0 gold, 45 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,700\n+75 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Move swiftly, ‹name›. Or is the task I requested too difficult?","done":"Excellent, ‹name›. In time, the land will heal. We must not give up.","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":75.8,"y":43.6,"n":"Rok Orhan","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"9295":{"id":9295,"t":"Letter from the Front","lv":60,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 45 instead of 55.","obj":"Take the Torn Letter to the Keeper of the Rolls at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nA Torn Letter\nProvided: A Torn Letter","desc":"You found this letter on one of the many Scourge minions you've slain. From its appearance and smell, it has been with the undead for some time. Perhaps someone at Light's Hope Chapel would be interested in examining it further...","back":"Yes? What do you have there?","done":"How tragic. These words, clearly meant for someone the soldier loved, never made it to their destination. The events detailed happened years ago; I'm not sure if the intended recipient still lives.\nThere is hope yet, however. With the names and information he gives, I might be able to locate the family! It will take some research, but the librarian in Stormwind owes me a favor...\nThank you for bringing this to me. With your help, we may be able to grant someone peace of mind at least.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.2,"y":50.6,"n":"Keeper of the Rolls","e":1}],"cats":["invasion"]},"255":{"id":255,"t":"Mercenaries","lv":19,"min":15,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays 20s instead of 11s.","obj":"Magistrate Bluntnose of Thelsamar has hired you to kill 4 Mo'grosh Ogres, 4 Mo'grosh Brutes and 4 Mo'grosh Enforcers.\nMo'grosh Ogre slain : 0/ 4\nMo'grosh Brute slain : 0/ 4\nMo'grosh Enforcer slain : 0/ 4","desc":"Two months just to hear from Ironforge that we'll be spared a handful of soldiers for our own defense, and another two months until they arrive! Bad enough that our town goes unprotected, but the excavation and the dam--the dam!--are open to attacks as well.\nI've no choice then, it seems. I'll need hired arms.\nHow about you? You seem a likely sort, ‹class›. A group of ogres has set up camp on the northeast of the lake. Perhaps you will be the one to remove the threat to our town?","rew":"Money: 20 0 gold, 20 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,800\n+150 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Have you had any luck?","done":"Ah, this is excellent news! Your efforts are greatly appreciated by myself and the people of Thelsamar. Better yet, if we can solve the ogre problem, we'll be able to shift our focus to those Light-burning troggs.","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":34.6,"y":44.5,"n":"Magistrate Bluntnose","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["loch-modan"]},"8735":{"id":8735,"t":"The Nightmare's Corruption","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to the four Emerald Dream portals in Azeroth and collect a Fragment of the Nightmare's Corruption from each. Return to Keeper Remulos in the Moonglade when you have completed this task.\nFragment of the Nightmare's Corruption Emeraldon Oracle 5 % , Emeraldon Tree Warder 5 % , Emeraldon Boughguard 5 %\nFragment of the Nightmare's Corruption Twilight Corrupter\nFragment of the Nightmare's Corruption Jademir Boughguard 5 % , Jademir Tree Warder 5 % , Jademir Oracle 5 %\nFragment of the Nightmare's Corruption Verdantine Tree Warder 5 % , Verdantine Oracle 5 % , Verdantine Boughguard 5 %","desc":"You must travel to the four dream portals of Azeroth. From each you must draw a fragment of the Nightmare's corruption. The dragonkin that inhabit these areas will hold such fragments. Return to me when you have gathered these fragments.","rew":"Experience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"<Remulos is lost deep in thought.>","done":"Are you prepared? Is the world prepared for what we are about to invoke? I do not know... I am bound by duty to Malfurion. Duty and honor...","pins":[{"z":"Moonglade","x":36.2,"y":41.8,"n":"Keeper Remulos","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["moonglade"]},"9055":{"id":9055,"t":"Cryptstalker Legguards","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Huntsman Leopold at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make Cryptstalker Legguards if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Legguards, 20 Wartorn Chain Scraps, 3 Arcanite Bars and 5 Cured Rugged Hides.\nDesecrated Legguards\n20 Wartorn Chain Scrap Stoneskin Gargoyle 14.4 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 13.5 % in Naxxramas , Spirit of Naxxramas 13.3 % in Naxxramas , Living Monstrosity 12.5 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\n3 Arcanite Bar\n5 Cured Rugged Hide","desc":"I have discovered a use for the carapace of the crypt fiend. I am able to fashion an extremely light and very deadly set of armor by combining the fragments with some of the desecrated magical armors lost in Naxxramas.\nBring me the items I require and I shall fashion for you a suit of armor the likes of which has never before been seen in our world!","rew":"You will receive:\nCryptstalker Legguards\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You got some missing parts for the quest please go and get them all!","done":"Exellent ‹name› !\n, you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Cryptstalker Legguards.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":48.9,"n":"Huntsman Leopold","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"8415":{"id":8415,"t":"Chillwind Point","lv":52,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Commander Ashlam Valorfist at Chillwind Camp.","desc":"Commander Ashlam Valorfist has sent out a call for a paladin of your purity and valor, ‹name›. You can find him at Chillwind Camp in the southern part of the Western Plaguelands. Seek him and aid in his cause for the Light!","rew":"Experience: 500","done":"Very well, ‹class›! Let's see what you're made of.\nStormwind City Western Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":48.4,"y":50.2,"n":"Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker","s":1},{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":42.7,"y":84,"n":"Commander Ashlam Valorfist","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"8255":{"id":8255,"t":"Of Coursers We Know","lv":52,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Acquire 4 Healthy Courser Glands and bring them to Ogtinc in Azshara. Ogtinc resides atop the cliffs northeast the Ruins of Eldarath.\n4 Healthy Courser Gland Mosshoof Courser 33 %","desc":"The mosshoof coursers of Azshara are magnificent animals who once lived in Felwood. They naturally resist disease and poison, and were unaffected by the corruption there. In their ancestral wisdom, they simply chose to leave that sickened place.\nIt saddens my heart, but I must ask you to hunt these mighty beasts for me. Gather four courser glands as the first ingredient for a restorative salve -- a salve we will use to heal Felwood.","rew":"Experience: 5,100","back":"You have returned. Were you successful?","done":"It is good the divine path has led you to us, ‹name›. Your beliefs do not interfere with the tasks involved in creating this salve.\nYou see, the courser is sacred to the Cenarion Circle, and killing them for any reason, no matter how necessary, weakens their spirit.","pins":[{"z":"Azshara","x":42.4,"y":42.6,"n":"Ogtinc","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"8815":{"id":8815,"t":"One Commendation Signet","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Horde Commendation Signet","back":"For those adventurers who have but a single commendation signet, I'll exchange it for a small amount of recognition with Orgrimmar.\nPlease bear in mind that it is better to hand over a stack of ten signets at once; your efforts will receive greater recognition in doing so. We offer a single signet exchange as a service for those who don't have enough for a full stack of ten.\nWith that being said, I stand ready to assist you if you still wish to hand in a single signet.","done":"Very well - your deeds have been entered into the records, and you are duly recognized for your efforts. Keep up the good work, ‹class›.\nIf you have any more signets to hand in, then I am able to assist you further in that regard.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":30.8,"y":73.7,"n":"Orgrimmar Commendation Officer","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":42.5,"y":38.7,"n":"Officer Redblade","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["reputation"]},"92415":{"id":92415,"t":"Remember That I Love You","lv":22,"min":15,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its experience counts the level 30 build, which halved what dungeon quests give beyond a normal quest.","obj":"Bring the Blood-Stained Letter to Orphan Matron Nightingale in Stormwind City.\nProvided: Blood-Stained Letter","desc":"<A torn and stained bundle of parchment has barely survived the undead trodden grounds of the graveyard. It mentions a missing child of the Heartweaver family. Perhaps the orphan matron in Stormwind City will know more.>","back":"What is it, Big? What are you looking for?","done":"Heartweaver? Heartweaver...\nOh! Little Jeremy Heartweaver. He was brought in years ago after the attack on Lordaeron. Lost both of his parents in the attack, poor thing.\nHe was actually adopted not too long ago by a sweet woman out in Duskwood.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":47.2,"y":38.4,"n":"Orphan Matron Nightingale","e":1}],"cats":["ruins-of-lordaeron-dungeon"]},"1535":{"id":1535,"t":"Call of Water","lv":22,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Fill the Empty Brown Waterskin at the watering hole below Brine's hut and return it to her in the Barrens.\nFilled Brown Waterskin\nProvided: Empty Brown Waterskin","desc":"To find understanding and gain the sapta from me, you must seek out only the purest forms of water. As you fetch the samples for me, take note of your surroundings. Be aware of the creatures that rely on the water, that protect it. See how it affects forests and deserts. Witness how the very substance that sustains life will force creatures to take lives.\nWe shall start with a simple task: down below my hut there is a pond of the precious liquid. Fill this skin with it and return to me.","rew":"Experience: 875","back":"I am just about prepared to send you on your other tasks. Have you filled the skin yet?\nI know how protective the quilboar can be. Even such a small water source is a vast hoard of wealth to them. They have great feasts when even the slightest rain comes to the Barrens. Water is sacred to their kind because it is so scarce. Do you understand?","done":"I thought some bloodshed might ensue if you tried to take water from the pool. It is a pity the quilboar do not realize that all living things are tied together; that their greed only perpetuates the pain and suffering of their people. How much could they accomplish if they were to put their differences aside and their clans came together.\nAgain, a pity, but more than likely a boon for the other races of the Barrens.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":43.4,"y":77.4,"n":"Brine","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"94495":{"id":94495,"t":"Call of water","lv":22,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Find Hervdana Saegrund in the Wetlands.","desc":"If there's one truth ye need to learn about water, it's this: water means rebirth. It carves stone, cleanses filth, and heals the weary -- but only when it's pure. Taint it, and it'll ruin all it touches.\nIf ye seek the water sapta, find Hervdana Saegrund in the Wetlands. Her family dwells in a cave beneath the southern falls.\nGo on then, don't let the river outrun ye.","done":"Aye, I see it in yer eyes, ‹race›. You're wonderin' what kind o' soul chooses to live out here, deep in the Wetlands, with Dark Iron scum lurkin' about and nary a guard in sight. Well, we all have our reasons, love.\nBut the real question is, what brings you to our home? Out here at the edge of the falls, I reckon we both know the answer to that.\nLoch Modan Wetlands","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":41.8,"y":19,"n":"Norric Lochthane","s":1},{"z":"Wetlands","x":65.6,"y":76.4,"n":"Hervdana Saegrund","e":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"79535":{"id":79535,"t":"Basilisks should petrification be feared","lv":35,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Basilisks: Should Petrification be Feared?","rew":"You will receive:\nItem 211779\nMoney: 3 50 0 gold, 3 silver, 50 copper Experience: 280","back":"Have you brought something to add to our collection?\nBasilisks: Should Petrification be Feared? (1)","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. Our knowledge expands through your efforts.\nIf you discover more magical works that might benefit the library, please bring them to me.\nStormwind City Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":37.8,"y":80.2,"n":"Garion Wendell","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":73.6,"y":33,"n":"Owen Thadd","e":1}],"cats":["special"]},"335":{"id":335,"t":"A Noble Brew","lv":30,"min":25,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Zardeth the Black Claw wants you to bring him a Tear of Tilloa from Darkshire and a Musquash Root from the Wetlands.\nTear of Tilloa Tear of Tilloa\nMusquash Root Musquash Root","desc":"Lord Wishock is causing quite a stir amongst the House of Nobles. He was made aware of our little \"establishment\" down here and is lobbying for a full investigation. I have a plan to keep Wishock \"preoccupied\", but I'll need your help.\nThere is a flower growing in the Garden of Stalvan on the outskirts of Darkshire. This small white flower is known as the Tear of Tilloa. I will also need a Musquash Root, found only at the very base of the falls far beneath the Stonewrought Dam in the Wetlands.","rew":"Money: 25 0 gold, 25 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,450","back":"Wishock will soon garner enough support to cause us much grief. Were you able to obtain the Tear of Tilloa or Musquash Root yet?","done":"Most excellent! These are fine samples indeed!\nStormwind City Duskwood Wetlands","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":40.1,"y":85.3,"n":"Zardeth of the Black Claw","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"575":{"id":575,"t":"Supply and Demand","lv":31,"min":26,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 2 Large River Crocolisk Skins to Drizzlik in Booty Bay.\n2 Large River Crocolisk Skin River Crocolisk 34 %","desc":"\"The finest leathercrafter of the South Seas and the worlds old and new.\" That's what they call me. Me! Drizzlik! The finest lea... Ahem. Well.\nMy leather goods are known far and wide as the most exquisite, a connoisseur's choice!\nI've just received an order from Director Riddlevox of the Tinkers' Union for a dozen of his favorite Excelsior-line boots. Our best sellers, actually.\nTo start on the basic shape, I'll need crocolisk skins from the crocs along the river in northern Stranglethorn.","rew":"Money: 22 0 gold, 22 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,250\n+100 reputation with Booty Bay\n-500 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","back":"My equipment is all ready to go, ‹name›, I just need those skins. We don't want to keep Riddlevox waiting, that's for sure.\nIt's not a good idea for anyone to keep the chief inventor of the Tinkers' Union unsatisfied.","done":"These skins should do. Their quality isn't too important, given that they'll make up the inside layer of the boots, but it's still important that they're comfortable.\nIf they're a bit too rigid, I'll use some tiger blood to soften it up. Tricks o' the trade, you know?","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":28.3,"y":77.6,"n":"Drizzlik","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"4495":{"id":4495,"t":"A Good Friend","lv":4,"min":2,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Iverron by the cave to the north.","desc":"A friend of mine named Iverron usually visits me at the same time every day. The strange thing is that he hasn't been by today at all -- he's several hours late, in fact.\nI admit, I am a little worried, ‹name›. Iverron spends a lot of time over by the cave to the north, and I'm sure you know how dangerous it is there -- spiders, everywhere!\nIf you happen to be going that way, though, will you keep an eye out for him?","rew":"Experience: 270\n+75 reputation with Darnassus","done":"I'm so glad you found me, ‹name›. How did you know I was here?","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":60.9,"y":42,"n":"Dirania Silvershine","s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":54.6,"y":33,"n":"Iverron","e":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"895":{"id":895,"t":"WANTED: Baron Longshore","lv":16,"min":11,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the head of Baron Longshore to Gazlowe in Ratchet.\nBaron Longshore's Head Baron Longshore","desc":"WANTED!\nBaron Longshore, Captain of the Heedless\nCaptain Longshore of Gilneas leads vessels of the Southsea Freebooters, and is wanted on charges of piracy. Remains must be in identifiable condition!\n-- Gazlowe","rew":"Money: 8 0 gold, 8 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,150\n+100 reputation with Ratchet","back":"What's happening? Something I can help you with? Goods to ship, perhaps an engineering job?","done":"Ahhhh! That sort of business. You know, I saw the Heedless once on the open seas. Fearsome ship, or was that boat... those sailors are so particular!\nAnyways, watching her glide across the water was quite a sight to see. I'm glad her infamous captain will trouble my ships no longer.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.6,"y":37.5,"n":"WANTED","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.7,"y":36.2,"n":"Gazlowe","e":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"98095":{"id":98095,"t":"Valuable vantages","lv":25,"min":19,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Deathstalker Masoj needs you to place the three Apothecary Vials on peaks around Hillsbrad Foothills and return to him.\nWestern vial placed\nNorthern vial placed\nSouthern vial placed","desc":"Our high command inserts strategic troops using bat riders. Key points around the foothills have lost their signaling beacons.\nTake these vials. Uncork them in three locations: the hills bordering Dun Garok, the plataeu overlooking Dunholde Keep, and the last on the ridge of the Headland above the town of Hillsbrad. The vapors that emanate will be like a potent tuning rod to the senses of the bat, drawing them to the desired drop-off points once more.\nLook for crushed empty vials and renew our marks.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nWeathered Deathstalker's Blade Expended Apothecary Vial\nExperience: 2,000\n+150 reputation with Thunder Bluff\nLevel 25 , requires level 19 Difficulty 19 21 23 28 33 Side Horde Shareable Yes Quest ID 98095\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 25, 4,000 XP in all.\n1 [ 25 ] Scout Support\nHigh Executor Darthalia wants you to deliver updated orders to Deathstalker Masoj, south of Tarren Mill, outside of Dun Garok\nHigh Executor Darthalia Hillsbrad Foothills\n2,000 XP\n2 [ 25 ] Valuable Vantages this quest\nDeathstalker Masoj needs you to place the three Apothecary Vials on peaks around Hillsbrad Foothills and return to him.\n2,000 XP","cats":["the-barrens"]},"96895":{"id":96895,"t":"The argent emissary","lv":13,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Find the Argent Dawn member near the entrance to the Undercity.","desc":"Not sure if you heard, but two emissaries of the Argent Dawn just passed through here. I don't mind the Argent Dawn, but I don't like them poking around Tirisfal unsupervised either. They were both Forsaken... but that doesn't make me any less nervous.\nOne of them just passed by here, headed southeast. There's a group of scourge cultists snooping around the outskirts of the city in that direction. If those two heard about them, there's no doubt that would have caught their attention.","rew":"Money: 3 0 gold, 3 silver, 0 copper Experience: 460\n+150 reputation with Argent Dawn","done":"Stay low and try not to be seen, ‹class›. These cultists are not to be trifled with.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.4,"y":53.4,"n":"Deathguard Terrence","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":65.8,"y":61,"n":"Hadric Harlson","e":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"3375":{"id":3375,"t":"Replacement Phial","lv":42,"min":37,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a Mana Potion, Coal, and Sweet Nectar to Talvash del Kissel in Ironforge to get a replacement for Talvash's Phial of Scrying.\nMana Potion Qiraji Captain Ka'ark 62.2 % , Skeletal Servant 40 % , Anubisath Warbringer 25 % , Qiraji Major 25 % and 4 more\nCoal Dalaran Miner , Blazing Elemental 28.4 % , Inferno Elemental 24.7 % , Molten Giant 24.7 % and 4 more\nSweet Nectar Dockmaster Baren , Healing Ward V , Dalaran Brewmaster , Barrel of Sweet Nectar and 4 more","desc":"Um... you need another phial of scrying? You're kidding, right? What did you do with the first one?! We have a lot of work ahead of us here, ‹race›. Those phials don't grow on trees! Actually, I wish they did, because I'd go there and pick one off since I don't have another one!!\nin order to make you one, I need the following: a mana potion, a piece of coal, and some sweet nectar. Don't ask why, just bring me what I ask and I'll make you a new one.","rew":"You will receive:\nTalvash's Phial of Scrying","back":"To make another phial I need a mana potion, a piece of coal, and some sweet nectar.\nThat, and a whole lotta patience apparently.","done":"The mighty adventurer delivers. Hooray for me. By the way, I lied - I had another phial. Ungh, take it.\nWell, what did you expect?! \"Oh, here, have another one! I'm just some goofball who has nothing better to do than hand out magical communication devices to adventurers!\" Rest assured though, what you have given to me will be enough make you another phial when you lose that too.\nPlease prove me wrong and don't lose the new one, okay?","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":56.9,"y":21.7,"n":"Talvash del Kissel","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["uldaman"]},"495":{"id":495,"t":"The Crown of Will","lv":39,"min":34,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Report to Melisara at Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills.","desc":"Mug'Thol and his ogre warband was sent to Alterac to retrieve the Crown of Will for Lady Sylvanas. Unfortunately, instead of returning it, the idiot decided to try it on... I suppose ogres can't resist anything bright and shiny.\nHis bumbling actions have become something of a problem, however. The Crown of Will enabled him to resist the possession placed upon him to serve Lady Sylvanas.\nThe Dark Lady wants an example made, travel to Tarren Mill in Hillsbrad and report to Melisara, my lieutenant.","rew":"Experience: 300","done":"You were sent by Shalindra? Very well then, you'll find I don't waste much time with idle chatter.\nMug'Thol is an irritant, and we will deal with him quickly, thoroughly, and without incident.\nUndercity Hillsbrad Foothills","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":57.6,"y":93.8,"n":"Sharlindra","s":1},{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":62.6,"y":20.6,"n":"Melisara","e":1}],"cats":["undercity"]},"98575":{"id":98575,"t":"Tainted tablet","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Read the Tainted Tablet and speak to Nartok inside the Den in the Valley of Trials.\nProvided: Tainted Tablet","desc":"Ah, while you were gone a tablet came for you, ‹name›.\nI usually avoid dealing with warlocks if I can help it, but I think you should read it when you have time. If I'm not mistaken, it came from your newly-appointed trainer, Nartok. He would have words with you when you're ready.","back":"Ah, you received my message. Excellent. We orcs have a long and turbulent history with the entities of the Nether, but now we forge our own path, in command of our destiny. You, too, can seize the power to shape the future for your people. Where our leaders falter, we are ready to press forward and claim our rightful place. You will be of eminence among the trolls.","done":"You have just glimpsed the power that can be yours. The feeble and foolish among us are afraid of the path that we tread, but with boldness and cunning we can decide our own fates.\nGuard your powers closely. The fearful lash out against that which they do not understand.\nNow you are one of us. If you need training in spells then return to me.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":42,"y":68.4,"n":"Gornek","s":1},{"z":"Durotar","x":40.6,"y":68.4,"n":"Nartok","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"4975":{"id":4975,"t":"The Completed Orb of Noh'Orahil","lv":40,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Wait for Menara Voidrender to complete the Orb of Noh'Orahil and then speak to her again.","desc":"I will get started immediately on crafting your orb and infusing your new demon into it. When done, you will have the choice of having it in the form of a staff or orb. I always felt it was important to cater to a warlock's chosen weapon... I see no reason not to continue that practice.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nOrb of Noh'Orahil Staff of Noh'Orahil\nExperience: 3,900","done":"It is done, ‹name›. Simply tell me which you'd prefer: a staff that would require you to use both hands, or an orb so you may use a dagger or sword as your weapon.\nTackling the infernal was a great feat on your part and this reward will fit you nicely. I wish you further success in the arts, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.5,"y":35.4,"n":"Menara Voidrender","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"5215":{"id":5215,"t":"The Scourge Cauldrons","lv":53,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with High Priestess MacDonnell at Chillwind Point, Western Plaguelands.","desc":"Within the lands of former Lordaeron are eight cauldrons - four here in the west, and four more ensconced in the east. These cauldrons spew poisons into the air, propagating the plague throughout the land for the Scourge.\nThe necromantic might of Kel'Thuzad is too strong to outright shut down these cauldrons, but we think we might have a way to subvert them to our advantage. My second, High Priestess MacDonnell, will be your point on this assignment; she'll continue the briefing from here.","rew":"Experience: 525\n+10 reputation with Stormwind","done":"May the power of the Light shine upon you in these dark times, ‹class›. I am pleased to serve as your coordinator for our plan to sabotage the Scourge's cauldrons.\nOur goal will be to change the composition of the plague that the cauldrons create into something that negatively affects the Scourge. In order to affect this change, you will need to secure access to each of the four cauldrons present in the Western Plaguelands.\nStand ready hero, for a glorious battle against the vile Scourge awaits you!","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":42.7,"y":84,"n":"Commander Ashlam Valorfist","s":1},{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":43,"y":84.5,"n":"High Priestess MacDonnell","e":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"5055":{"id":5055,"t":"Brumeran of the Chillwind","lv":58,"min":53,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Storm Shadowhoof at Everlook in Winterspring wants you to kill Brumeran.\nBrumeran slain","desc":"Swift, and clever, Brumeran glides silently across the snowy landscape of southern Winterspring. But do not let her graceful appearance convince you that she is harmless. All that cross her pay considerably, and often with their own lives.\nSeek out Brumeran of the chillwind among the chimera. Defeat her, then return again to me.","rew":"Experience: 6,200\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Brumeran calls out to you, ‹name›.","done":"Yes. You have returned. I believe now that you are a true ‹class› by nature. You have faced the most ferocious of creatures and have returned, surpassing my expectations.\nYou are now ready for my final request.","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":61.9,"y":38.4,"n":"Storm Shadowhoof","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"975":{"id":975,"t":"Cache of Mau'ari","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Witch Doctor Mau'ari again in a moment to receive the lucky charm.","desc":"Now, before I give ya dis charm, I better explain how ta use it.\nIf you carry da charm with ya, you'll find dat certain items will drop from creatures ya fight. If you don't have da charm with you, you won't find them. Understand?\nYou'll know these special items by the name -- they be called E'ko. If you find any of these items, just bring dem to ol' Mau'ari, and she help ya out.\nWait here while I fix your charm.","rew":"You will receive:\nCache of Mau'ari","done":"Here it is, ‹name›. Remember, ya have ta carry it with you. Why don't ya head back to Winterspring, an' see what ya be findin' there?","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":61.9,"y":38.3,"n":"Witch Doctor Mau'ari","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]}});